---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import sources from "../data/sources.json";
---
<Base title="Sources">
  <h1>Sources</h1>
  <p class="lede">What has been read, and where it is.</p>
  {sources.map(s => (
    <section class="card" style="margin:.9rem 0">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:.3rem">{s.t}</h3>
      <p style="margin:0">{s.d}</p>
    </section>
  ))}
  <h2>Records cited in the direct line</h2>
  <p>Twenty-six record citations underlie the pedigree, drawn from three civil collections and the Arienzo
  parish books. They are listed in full in <span class="mono">data/record-citations.tsv</span> in the
  repository, with the archival reference for each.</p>
  <h2>Not yet reached</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The Arienzo baptism register of <strong>1672–1738</strong> — unexamined. This is where a generation
    above Pasquale Falco would be found, if it is to be found at all.</li>
    <li>The <strong>marriage supplements</strong> (<em>processetti</em>) for Arienzo. These attach earlier
    documents — often parish extracts reaching back two generations — to a marriage file, and are the
    single richest source for pushing past 1809.</li>
    <li>The <strong>Archdiocese of Benevento</strong> church records, 1575–1908, for the Arpaia and Forchia
    years and the Zampiello family.</li>
    <li>Certain FamilySearch record images for Caserta are restricted to accounts at a FamilySearch centre
    or affiliate library, and could not be opened for this build.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
